---
description: Avoid misaligned buttons and controls in flex rows, modals, and cards
alwaysApply: true
---

# Button and Control Alignment

Global `button, .btn` in `global.templ` sets `margin-top: var(--space-5)`, large padding, and filled primary styling. `.add-btn` resets `margin-top: 0`, but `.btn` / `.btn-secondary` do not.

Mixing those classes in one row is the most common cause of misaligned UI.

Global `.modal-footer` in `global.templ` sets `display: flex`, `gap: var(--space-3)`, `padding: var(--space-3) var(--space-4) var(--space-4)`, `border-top`, and `margin-top: 0` on footer buttons. **Put footer buttons as direct children of `.modal-footer`**. Wrapping them in an inner div breaks the global gap unless that wrapper is also a flex row with gap.

Form-wrapped modals must keep `.modal-footer` as a sibling of `.modal-body` inside the `<form>`. Global `.modal-dialog > form` is already `display: flex; flex-direction: column`.

## Flex rows with multiple controls

Any horizontal group of buttons or icon actions (modal footers, card actions, toolbars) needs:

```css
.my-footer,
.my-footer-actions,
.my-card-actions {
	display: flex;
	flex-wrap: wrap;
	align-items: center;
	gap: var(--space-2);
}

.my-footer button,
.my-footer .btn,
.my-footer .add-btn {
	margin-top: 0;
}
```

Apply the `margin-top: 0` reset to **every** button class in the row, not only `.add-btn`.

Reference: `.lm-form-footer` / `.tm-form-footer` in `learning_materials.templ` and `training_materials.templ`.

## Text buttons beside icon actions

`.icon-action-btn` is fixed at `36px` height with `margin-top: 0`. A nearby `.btn` or `button` will look taller and sit off baseline unless you normalize it:

```css
.my-card-actions .btn {
	display: inline-flex;
	align-items: center;
	justify-content: center;
	height: 36px;
	margin-top: 0;
	padding: 0 var(--space-3);
	font-size: 0.8125rem;
	line-height: 1;
	box-sizing: border-box;
}
```

Reference: `.tm-card-actions .btn` in `training_materials.templ`.

## Chip and tag remove buttons

Do not use bare `button` for chip × controls. Use the global reset in `global.templ` (`button.lm-tag-chip-remove`, `button.chip-remove`, etc.) or match that pattern with a `button.` compound selector so global button padding/background/margin do not leak through.

Parent chip: `display: inline-flex; align-items: center; gap: …`.

## Head scripts

Inline scripts in `<head>` (`GlobalIncludes`) run before `<body>` exists. Never call `document.body.addEventListener` without a guard or `DOMContentLoaded` deferral. See `ScrTableTruncationTooltips` in `scripts.templ`.

## Checklist for new UI

- [ ] Footer/action row uses `display: flex; align-items: center`
- [ ] All buttons in the row have `margin-top: 0`
- [ ] Mixed `.btn` + `.icon-action-btn` rows share the same height (usually `36px`)
- [ ] Chip remove buttons use the global chip-remove reset, not default `button` styles
